---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import IndexLayout from "../../layouts/IndexLayout.astro";
import Contents from "../../components/Contents.astro";
import { contentUrl, directContentChildren } from "../../lib/content";
const entries = directContentChildren(await getCollection("beyond", ({ data }) => !data.draft && data.lang === "en"));
const items = entries.map((entry) => ({
  href: contentUrl("beyond", entry.id, "en"),
  label: entry.data.title,
}));
---

<IndexLayout title="Beyond">
  <p>There is an inner conner, and I don't know how to define it accurately. Benjamin once used the name of "one way street" to describe his inner feeling. Maybe you can view the contents as a space for thoughts and reflections, or personally interpreted wiki, or just the world from another eyes.</p>
  <Contents items={items} />
</IndexLayout>
